recently i posted the idea that nethack 3.1 should be
user-configurable for screen size in order to get
larger level sizes for those who have spiffier
terminals.  it was pointed out that this might cause a
disruption in game balance (yeah, as if that was a
consideration for improving nethack  :-)  ).

i still believe that it is a modification that will
improve the game dramatically (for some) yet involve
relatively little hacking with the code.  and it need
not affect game balance that much.  it is true that
someone with a 135x60 screen, if there are still around
24 "regular" levels, would have an inordinate advantage
over people with lowly 80x24's, since they'd have more
space to search and more items to find.  but there's no
reason to give these mega-terminal people all 24 or so
levels.  if someone has twice as much screen space as
normal (say 80x50, which ibm vga's can get in text
mode), half the number of levels 'till medusa.  it's an
easy mathematical relationship that any dumb computer
can get in one function:  medusalevel = f(rows,
columns).

hmm.  class begins.  anyway, there it is.

